EXPECTED: CONFIRMED_DOS
CVE: CVE-2026-71249

ATTACK: DNS-over-TLS CPU flood — 50 persistent TLS connections each pipelining queries continuously
DOS_CLASS: cpu

TARGET_IMAGE: coredns/coredns:1.11.3
TARGET_PORT: 853/tcp
TLS: self-signed (infra/certs/)
CLIENT_TOOL: ssl + socket (struct-encoded DNS wire format)

FINDING_TYPE: SecurityDesignGap

PROOF_METHOD: metric
PROOF_METRIC: cpu_pct
PROOF_THRESHOLD: +50pp CPU sustained 5s
PROOF_NOTES: CoreDNS tls server with erratic backend (immediate responses).
             50 persistent TLS connections pipeline queries at ~8000/s.
             Each query requires TLS decrypt + DNS parse + erratic lookup + DNS encode + TLS encrypt.
             Control: same 50 TLS connections held without queries → near-zero CPU.
             Differential confirms query processing (not connection overhead) saturates single-vCPU.
             No per-IP query-rate limit enforced by default.
